:-webkit-match-parent] supports-[text-align:match-parent]:[text-align:match-parent]">Searched the web, updated memory</span></span></span></span><button type="button" data-cds-row-toggle="" data-cds-row-toggle-stretched="" class="cds-reset -ms-1 inline-flex h-[1lh] shrink-0 items-center self-start border-0 bg-transparent p-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden static justify-center after:absolute after:inset-0 after:rounded-[var(--cds-row-radius,var(--cds-radius))] after:content-[''] after:transition-shadow after:duration-fast focus-visible:after:[box-shadow:inset_0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-focus-width,1px)_var(--cds-fill-accent)]" tabindex="0" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" aria-labelledby="_r_31m_-label" aria-owns="_r_31m_-label"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-flex h-[1lh] items-center justify-center text-secondary group-hover/status:text-secondary group-focus-visible/status-line:text-secondary group-has-[:focus-visible]/status-line:text-secondary"><span data-cds="Icon" class="transition-transform duration-fast motion-reduce:transition-none -rotate-90 page-rtl:rotate-90" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 433.3; width: 0.6em; height: 0.6em; contain: layout paint; pointer-events: none; translate: 0px 0.5px;"></span></span></button></div><span class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div><div data-transcript-engine-root="" class="contents"><div data-cds="Prose" data-prose-heading-size="sm" data-prose-tables="flat" class="prose stacks:[&amp;_li:not(:where([data-cds-theme]_*:not([data-cds-unthemed]_*)))::marker]:[--cds-text-secondary:currentColor]" style="--_prose-font-body: var(--font-claude-response, var(--cds-font-voice)); --_prose-font-heading-display: var(--_prose-font-heading);"><div data-perf-reply-text="" class="_blocks_ta2es_47 standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 whitespace-normal break-words print:block"><h2 dir="ltr" aria-level="4">dbt + DuckDB Project: Step-by-Step (Olist E-commerce)</h2>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>What you’ll build:</strong> a local analytics warehouse. Raw CSVs go in, dbt turns them into tested staging models, a star schema (facts and dimensions), and a small dashboard.</p>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Time:</strong> plan about 1.5 days since you’re learning. The 8-hour version assumes you’ve used dbt before.</p>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">What I verified, and what changed from my earlier plan</h3>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><strong>dbt Core only.</strong> DuckDB works with the dbt Core command line, not the hosted dbt platform. That’s fine, everything below is CLI. <span data-not-prose=""><span class="inline-flex" id="base-ui-_r_31u_"><a href="https://docs.getdbt.com/guides/duckdb?step=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group/tag relative h-[18px] rounded-full inline-flex items-center overflow-hidden -translate-y-px cursor-pointer"><span class="relative transition-colors h-full max-w-[180px] overflow-hidden px-1.5 inline-flex items-center text-caption-regular font-sans rounded-full border-0.5 border-border-300 bg-bg-200 group-hover/tag:bg-accent-900 group-hover/tag:border-accent-100/60 stacks:group-hover/tag:bg-page stacks:group-hover/tag:layers-1-accent stacks:group-hover/tag:border-transparent"><span dir="auto" class="text-nowrap text-text-300 font-normal group-hover/tag:text-text-200 break-all truncate">getdbt</span></span><span class="transition-opacity opacity-[0%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] h-[17px] absolute right-[0.5px] rounded-r-full flex items-center px-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-900/0 via-accent-900/100 via-30% to-accent-900/100 [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:right-auto [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:left-[0.5px] [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-r-none [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-l-full [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:bg-gradient-to-l stacks:bg-page stacks:layers-1-accent stacks:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,transparent,black_30%)] stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:layers-1-accent stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_left,transparent,black_30%)]"><span data-cds="Icon" data-cds-mirror="" class="transition-[opacity,scale,transform] group-hover/tag:ease-out duration-[500ms] ease-in text-accent-100 group-hover/tag:scale-[100%] scale-[80%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] opacity-[0%]" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 533.3;"></span></span></a></span></span></li>
<li><strong>Where the data lives.</strong> DuckDB stores everything in one local <code dir="ltr">.duckdb</code> file, set by the <code dir="ltr">path</code> in <code dir="ltr">profiles.yml</code>. There’s no server and no account. <span data-not-prose=""><span class="inline-flex" id="base-ui-_r_322_"><a href="https://docs.getdbt.com/guides/duckdb?step=4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group/tag relative h-[18px] rounded-full inline-flex items-center overflow-hidden -translate-y-px cursor-pointer"><span class="relative transition-colors h-full max-w-[180px] overflow-hidden px-1.5 inline-flex items-center text-caption-regular font-sans rounded-full border-0.5 border-border-300 bg-bg-200 group-hover/tag:bg-accent-900 group-hover/tag:border-accent-100/60 stacks:group-hover/tag:bg-page stacks:group-hover/tag:layers-1-accent stacks:group-hover/tag:border-transparent"><span dir="auto" class="text-nowrap text-text-300 font-normal group-hover/tag:text-text-200 break-all truncate">getdbt</span></span><span class="transition-opacity opacity-[0%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] h-[17px] absolute right-[0.5px] rounded-r-full flex items-center px-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-900/0 via-accent-900/100 via-30% to-accent-900/100 [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:right-auto [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:left-[0.5px] [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-r-none [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-l-full [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:bg-gradient-to-l stacks:bg-page stacks:layers-1-accent stacks:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,transparent,black_30%)] stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:layers-1-accent stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_left,transparent,black_30%)]"><span data-cds="Icon" data-cds-mirror="" class="transition-[opacity,scale,transform] group-hover/tag:ease-out duration-[500ms] ease-in text-accent-100 group-hover/tag:scale-[100%] scale-[80%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] opacity-[0%]" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 533.3;"></span></span></a></span></span></li>
<li><strong>Package name changed.</strong> I earlier said <code dir="ltr">calogica/dbt_expectations</code>. The <code dir="ltr">metaplane/dbt_expectations</code> fork is the one the dbt package hub lists as compatible with newer dbt versions, while the calogica version requires dbt below 2.0. Use metaplane. The test names are the same. <span data-not-prose=""><span class="inline-flex" id="base-ui-_r_326_"><a href="https://hub.getdbt.com/calogica/dbt_expectations/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group/tag relative h-[18px] rounded-full inline-flex items-center overflow-hidden -translate-y-px cursor-pointer"><span class="relative transition-colors h-full max-w-[180px] overflow-hidden px-1.5 inline-flex items-center text-caption-regular font-sans rounded-full border-0.5 border-border-300 bg-bg-200 group-hover/tag:bg-accent-900 group-hover/tag:border-accent-100/60 stacks:group-hover/tag:bg-page stacks:group-hover/tag:layers-1-accent stacks:group-hover/tag:border-transparent"><span dir="auto" class="text-nowrap text-text-300 font-normal group-hover/tag:text-text-200 break-all truncate">getdbt</span></span><span class="transition-opacity opacity-[0%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] h-[17px] absolute right-[0.5px] rounded-r-full flex items-center px-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-900/0 via-accent-900/100 via-30% to-accent-900/100 [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:right-auto [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:left-[0.5px] [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-r-none [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-l-full [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:bg-gradient-to-l stacks:bg-page stacks:layers-1-accent stacks:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,transparent,black_30%)] stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:layers-1-accent stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_left,transparent,black_30%)]"><span data-cds="Icon" data-cds-mirror="" class="transition-[opacity,scale,transform] group-hover/tag:ease-out duration-[500ms] ease-in text-accent-100 group-hover/tag:scale-[100%] scale-[80%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] opacity-[0%]" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 533.3;"></span></span></a></span></span></li>
<li><strong>Incremental strategy.</strong> I said “merge” earlier. The safest default on dbt-duckdb is <code dir="ltr">delete+insert</code>. It behaves the same when you set a <code dir="ltr">unique_key</code>. Newer adapter versions also offer <code dir="ltr">merge</code>, so check the dbt-duckdb docs if you want to try it.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Concepts mapped to what you know</h3>
<div dir="ltr" class="md-table-scroll prose-scroll print:overflow-x-visible touch:scroll-fade-x focus-visible:mask-none [:root:not([dir=rtl])_&amp;:dir(rtl)]:mask-none"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col" style="min-width: 201px;">dbt concept</th><th scope="col" style="min-width: 530px;">Informatica-world equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Source</td><td>Source definition / landing table</td></tr><tr><td>Staging model</td><td>Source qualifier + light expression transforms</td></tr><tr><td>Intermediate / mart model</td><td>Mapping logic and target tables</td></tr><tr><td><code dir="ltr">ref()</code></td><td>Dependency between mappings (dbt builds the run order for you)</td></tr><tr><td>Tests</td><td>Validation rules and reject checks</td></tr><tr><td>Snapshot</td><td>SCD Type 2 mapping</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Phase 0: Setup (45 min)</h3>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Create a GitHub repo <code dir="ltr">olist-dbt-warehouse</code>, clone it, and <code dir="ltr">cd</code> into it.</li>
<li>Create the environment and install:</li>
</ol>
