text-[length:var(--msg-code-block-size,0.875rem)] !leading-relaxed p-3.5" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240); background: transparent; font-family: var(--font-mono);"><code class="language-python" data-highlight="final" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240); background: transparent; font-family: var(--font-mono); white-space: pre;"><span class="block [unicode-bidi:inherit] [text-align:-webkit-match-parent] [text-align:match-parent]" data-code-line-group=""><span><span><span style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">import</span> duckdb<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">,</span> pathlib
</span><span>
</span><span>con = duckdb<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>connect<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"olist/olist.duckdb"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>con<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>execute<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS raw"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">for</span> f <span style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">in</span><span style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);"> sorted</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span>pathlib<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>Path<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"data"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">).</span>glob<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"*.csv"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)):</span>
</span><span>    name = f<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>stem<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>replace<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"olist_"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">,</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);"> ""</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">).</span>replace<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"_dataset"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">,</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);"> ""</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>    con<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>execute<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">f</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"""</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">        CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE raw.</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">{</span>name<span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">}</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);"> AS</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">        SELECT *, current_timestamp AS _loaded_at</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">        FROM read_csv_auto('</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">{</span>f<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>as_posix<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">()</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">}</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">')</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">    """</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>    n = con<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>execute<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">f</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"SELECT count(*) FROM raw.</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">{</span>name<span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">}</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">).</span>fetchone<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">()[</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">]</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">    print</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(204, 123, 244);">f</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"raw.</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">{</span>name<span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">}</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">: </span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">{</span>n<span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">}</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);"> rows"</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>con<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span>close<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">()</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<ol dir="ltr" start="3">
<li>Run <code dir="ltr">python load_raw.py</code>. Sanity-check the counts against what other Olist projects report: about 103,886 payments, 99,224 reviews, 32,951 products, 3,095 sellers, and roughly 1 million geolocation rows. <span data-not-prose=""><span class="inline-flex" id="base-ui-_r_32k_"><a href="https://github.com/DevonSLran/Data_Engineering-Final_Project" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group/tag relative h-[18px] rounded-full inline-flex items-center overflow-hidden -translate-y-px cursor-pointer"><span class="relative transition-colors h-full max-w-[180px] overflow-hidden px-1.5 inline-flex items-center text-caption-regular font-sans rounded-full border-0.5 border-border-300 bg-bg-200 group-hover/tag:bg-accent-900 group-hover/tag:border-accent-100/60 stacks:group-hover/tag:bg-page stacks:group-hover/tag:layers-1-accent stacks:group-hover/tag:border-transparent"><span dir="auto" class="text-nowrap text-text-300 font-normal group-hover/tag:text-text-200 break-all truncate">github</span></span><span class="transition-opacity opacity-[0%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] h-[17px] absolute right-[0.5px] rounded-r-full flex items-center px-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-900/0 via-accent-900/100 via-30% to-accent-900/100 [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:right-auto [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:left-[0.5px] [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-r-none [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:rounded-l-full [&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:bg-gradient-to-l stacks:bg-page stacks:layers-1-accent stacks:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,transparent,black_30%)] stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:layers-1-accent stacks:[&amp;:where(:root[dir=rtl]_:dir(rtl))]:[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_left,transparent,black_30%)]"><span data-cds="Icon" data-cds-mirror="" class="transition-[opacity,scale,transform] group-hover/tag:ease-out duration-[500ms] ease-in text-accent-100 group-hover/tag:scale-[100%] scale-[80%] group-hover/tag:opacity-[100%] opacity-[0%]" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 533.3;"></span></span></a></span></span></li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr">Two gotchas:</p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li>If the reviews file errors on parsing (it has free-text comments with line breaks), add <code dir="ltr">, ignore_errors=true</code> inside <code dir="ltr">read_csv_auto(...)</code> and note it in your README.</li>
<li>DuckDB allows one writer at a time. Don’t run <code dir="ltr">load_raw.py</code> while dbt is running, and close any DuckDB UI or CLI first.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Done when:</strong> 9 tables exist in the <code dir="ltr">raw</code> schema.</p>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Phase 2: Sources and staging (1.5 hrs)</h3>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Learn:</strong> staging models should only rename, cast, and clean. No joins, no business logic.</p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Install packages. Create <code dir="ltr">olist/packages.yml</code>:</li>
</ol>
