<p dir="ltr">Reviews are known to have repeated <code dir="ltr">review_id</code> values. If you add a <code dir="ltr">unique</code> test on it and it fails, that’s a real finding about the data. Use a combination test on <code dir="ltr">review_id</code> + <code dir="ltr">order_id</code> instead, and note it in your README.</p>
<ol dir="ltr" start="5">
<li>Run <code dir="ltr">dbt build --select staging</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Done when:</strong> 8 staging views build and their tests pass.</p>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Phase 3: Intermediate and marts (2 hrs)</h3>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Learn:</strong> decide the grain first (what one row represents), then write the SQL.</p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li><code dir="ltr">olist/models/intermediate/int_orders_enriched.sql</code>. Grain: one row per order.</li>
</ol>
