</span><span><span style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">git</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);"> config --global user.email "you@example.com"</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Step 1: Create the repo on GitHub</h3>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Sign in at github.com. Click the <strong>+</strong> icon (top right) → <strong>New repository</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Repository name:</strong> <code dir="ltr">olist-dbt-warehouse</code></li>
<li><strong>Visibility:</strong> Public (recruiters can only see it if it’s public).</li>
<li>Check <strong>Add a README file</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Add .gitignore:</strong> choose the <strong>Python</strong> template. You’ll add a few project-specific lines later.</li>
<li>Skip the license for now.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Create repository</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Step 2: Clone it to your computer</h3>
<p dir="ltr">On the repo page, click the green <strong>Code</strong> button and copy the <strong>HTTPS</strong> URL. It looks like <code dir="ltr">https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/olist-dbt-warehouse.git</code>.</p>
<p dir="ltr">In your terminal, go to the folder where you keep projects (for example <code dir="ltr">cd ~/Documents</code>), then run:</p>
