<p dir="ltr">You should see <code dir="ltr">README.md</code> and a hidden <code dir="ltr">.gitignore</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Step 3: Sign in when Git asks</h3>
<p dir="ltr">For HTTPS, GitHub doesn’t accept your account password on the command line. If prompted, you have two easy options:</p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><strong>GitHub CLI (easiest):</strong> install it from cli.github.com, run <code dir="ltr">gh auth login</code>, and follow the prompts. After that, clones and pushes just work.</li>
<li><strong>Personal access token:</strong> GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens. Create one with the <code dir="ltr">repo</code> scope and paste it when Git asks for a password.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Step 4: Continue with Phase 0</h3>
<p dir="ltr">You’re now inside the repo folder, which is where the next steps start (<code dir="ltr">python -m venv .venv</code>, and so on). One thing to adjust: since you created the <code dir="ltr">.gitignore</code> from the Python template, just <em>append</em> the project lines instead of replacing the file:</p>
