md pointer-coarse:backdrop-blur-md [@media(hover:none)]:backdrop-blur-md" aria-label="Copy to clipboard" data-testid="code-block-copy" id="_r_2q0_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger="" fdprocessedid="r3qe4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow] stacks:transition-[box-shadow] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer  "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 433.3;"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></div></div><div class="text-secondary text-caption-regular font-sans p-3.5 pb-0 print:break-after-avoid" data-find-omitted="">markdown</div><div class="overflow-x-auto print:overflow-x-clip"><pre class="code-block__code !my-0 !rounded-[var(--msg-block-radius,0.5rem)] !text-[length:var(--msg-code-block-size,0.875rem)] !leading-relaxed p-3.5 print:!break-inside-auto print:overflow-clip" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240); background: transparent; font-family: var(--font-mono);"><code class="language-markdown" data-highlight="final" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240); background: transparent; font-family: var(--font-mono); white-space: pre;"><span class="block [unicode-bidi:inherit] [text-align:-webkit-match-parent] [text-align:match-parent]" data-code-line-group=""><span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">#</span> NYC Taxi + Weather Lakehouse (Databricks)
</span><span>
</span><span>A medallion-architecture pipeline on Databricks Free Edition that studies how weather affects NYC yellow taxi demand.
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> What this project demonstrates
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Incremental ingestion with Auto Loader into Delta tables
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Medallion layers (bronze, silver, gold) with Lakeflow Declarative Pipelines
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Data quality expectations (drop vs. warn) and a DQ metrics table built from the pipeline event log
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> A scheduled Workflow: ingest, pipeline, quality gate
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> A dashboard on the gold tables
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Architecture
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">```</span>mermaid
</span><span>flowchart LR
</span><span>    A[TLC trips parquet] --&gt; V[(Unity Catalog Volume)]
</span><span>    B[Open-Meteo weather JSON] --&gt; V
</span><span>    C[Zone lookup CSV] --&gt; V
</span><span>    V --&gt; D[Bronze: Auto Loader]
</span><span>    D --&gt; E[Silver: cleaned, expectations]
</span><span>    E --&gt; F[Gold: demand by zone-hour, revenue by weather]
</span><span>    E --&gt; Q[DQ check task]
</span><span>    F --&gt; G[Dashboard]
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">```</span>
</span><span>
</span><span>Pipeline graph:
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">![</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">Pipeline</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">](</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">docs/images/pipeline.png</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Data
</span><span>
</span></span></span><span class="block [unicode-bidi:inherit] [text-align:-webkit-match-parent] [text-align:match-parent]" data-code-line-group=""><span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> NYC TLC Yellow Taxi trips: &lt;months used&gt;, &lt;row count from your run&gt; rows
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Hourly temperature and precipitation for NYC from the Open-Meteo archive API (<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>timezone=America/New_York<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>)
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> TLC taxi zone lookup
</span><span>
</span><span>Source files are not stored in this repo.
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Tech stack
</span><span>
</span><span>Databricks Free Edition (serverless), Delta Lake, Auto Loader, Lakeflow Declarative Pipelines, Unity Catalog, Databricks Workflows, Databricks SQL dashboard
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Layers
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Layer <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Objects <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Notes <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|---|---|---|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Bronze <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">| `</span>bronze_trips<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>, <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>bronze_weather<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>, <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>bronze_zones<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">` |</span> Raw data plus <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>_ingested_at<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> and <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>_source_file<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">` |</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Silver <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">| `</span>silver_trips<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>, <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>silver_weather<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">` |</span> Typed, validated with expectations <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Gold <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">| `</span>gold_demand_by_zone_hour<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>, <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>gold_revenue_by_weather<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">` |</span> Demand and revenue joined to weather <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Data quality
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Rule <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Condition <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> Action <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|---|---|---|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> valid_fare <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">| `</span>fare_amount &gt;= 0<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">` |</span> drop row <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> valid_times <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> dropoff after pickup <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> drop row <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> valid_distance <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">| `</span>0 &lt; trip_distance &lt; 100<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">` |</span> drop row <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> valid_passengers <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">| `</span>passenger_count<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> between 1 and 6 <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span> warn only <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">|</span>
</span><span>
</span><span>Per-rule results are written to <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>dq_metrics_event_log<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> by the <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>dq_check<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> task, which fails the job if any rule's fail rate exceeds &lt;threshold&gt;. &lt;insert screenshot of the failed run you triggered on purpose&gt;
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Workflow
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>ingest/bronze<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> then <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>taxi_pipeline<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> then <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>dq_check<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>, scheduled &lt;daily/manual&gt;.
</span></span></span><span class="block [unicode-bidi:inherit] [text-align:-webkit-match-parent] [text-align:match-parent]" data-code-line-group=""><span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">![</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">Job run</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">](</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">docs/images/job_run.png</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Design decisions
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">- **</span>Manual file upload:<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">**</span> Free Edition restricts outbound internet from compute, so source files are downloaded locally and uploaded to a Volume.
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">- **</span>Incremental loads:<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">**</span> Auto Loader with <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>availableNow<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span> processes only new files. I verified this by adding a file and confirming only it was processed.
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">- **</span>Timezone:<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">**</span> TLC timestamps are local NYC time, so the weather request uses <span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>timezone=America/New_York<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">`</span>. A mismatch would silently skew the weather join.
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">- **</span>Drop vs. warn:<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">**</span> impossible values (negative fares, reversed timestamps) are dropped; passenger count only warns because it is often legitimately unrecorded.
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">- **</span>DQ gate:<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">**</span> the threshold of &lt;value&gt; was chosen after observing normal fail rates of &lt;values&gt;.
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">- **</span>Performance note:<span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">**</span> &lt;only include if you measured it, with real before/after timings&gt;
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Dashboard
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">![</span><span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">Dashboard</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">](</span><span style="color: rgb(94, 237, 237);">docs/images/dashboard.png</span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span>
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Limitations
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Free Edition compute quotas and a single active pipeline
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Only &lt;N&gt; months of data
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Weather is one point for all of NYC, not per zone
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">##</span> Possible next steps
</span><span>
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> Databricks Asset Bundles and CI deployment
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> SCD Type 2 zone dimension
</span><span><span style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">-</span> More months of data and a Z-ORDER comparison</span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<hr>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Part 3: Upload the dbt project to GitHub</h3>
<p dir="ltr">You cloned the repo earlier, so your project folder is already connected to GitHub. You just need to commit and push.</p>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Step 1: Check what Git sees</h4>
<p dir="ltr">Open a terminal in the repo root (the folder with <code dir="ltr">load_raw.py</code>) and run:</p>
<div data-not-prose=""><div role="group" aria-label="powershell code" tabindex="0" dir="ltr" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-[var(--msg-block-radius,0.5rem)] focus-visible:outline-hidden focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="static opacity-0 transition-[position] transition-discrete duration-0 delay-300 group-hover/copy:sticky group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-hover/copy:delay-0 group-focus-within/copy:sticky group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:delay-0 pointer-coarse:sticky pointer-coarse:opacity-100 [@media(hover:none)]:sticky [@media(max-resolution:1.99dppx)]:sticky [@media(hover:none)]:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 rounded-[calc(var(--cds-radius)+var(--cds-button-radius-add,0px))] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-text-button-icon-disabled)] group-hover/copy:backdrop-blur-md group-focus-within/copy:backdrop-blur-md pointer-coarse:backdrop-blur-md [@media(hover:none)]:backdrop-blur-md" aria-label="Copy to clipboard" data-testid="code-block-copy" id="_r_2q5_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger="" fdprocessedid="9mrge"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow] stacks:transition-[box-shadow] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer  "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1)); font-weight: 433.3;"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></div></div><div class="text-secondary text-caption-regular font-sans p-3.5 pb-0 print:break-after-avoid" data-find-omitted="">powershell</div><div class="overflow-x-auto"><pre class="code-block__code !my-0 !rounded-[var(--msg-block-radius,0.5rem)] !text-[length:var(--msg-code-block-size,0.875rem)] !leading-relaxed p-3.5" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240); background: transparent; font-family: var(--font-mono);"><code class="language-powershell" data-highlight="final" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240); background: transparent; font-family: var(--font-mono); white-space: pre;"><span class="block [unicode-bidi:inherit] [text-align:-webkit-match-parent] [text-align:match-parent]" data-code-line-group=""><span><span>git status</span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<p dir="ltr">You should see your new files in red, such as <code dir="ltr">README.md</code>, <code dir="ltr">olist/</code>, <code dir="ltr">app.py</code>. You should <strong>not</strong> see <code dir="ltr">data/</code>, <code dir="ltr">.venv/</code>, <code dir="ltr">olist.duckdb</code>, <code dir="ltr">olist/target/</code>, or <code dir="ltr">olist/dbt_packages/</code>. If you do, your <code dir="ltr">.gitignore</code> is missing those lines. Add them (they’re listed in the earlier Phase 0 instructions), save, and run <code dir="ltr">git status</code> again.</p>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Step 2: Check for secrets and large files</h4>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li>No Kaggle keys, passwords, or tokens in any file.</li>
<li><code dir="ltr">olist/profiles.yml</code> is safe to commit because it only holds a local file path. If you later add cloud credentials, never commit those.</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Step 3: Add your screenshots</h4>
<p dir="ltr">Create the folder <code dir="ltr">docs/images/</code> and save your screenshots there: <code dir="ltr">lineage.png</code>, <code dir="ltr">dashboard.png</code>, and any others you referenced.</p>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Step 4: Stage, commit, push</h4>
