</span><span>git push</span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<p dir="ltr">Windows may print “LF will be replaced by CRLF” warnings. They’re harmless.</p>
<p dir="ltr">If Git asks you to sign in, use the GitHub CLI (<code dir="ltr">gh auth login</code>) or a personal access token, as covered when you cloned.</p>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Step 5: Verify on GitHub</h4>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Open <code dir="ltr">https://github.com/&lt;YOUR-USERNAME&gt;/olist-dbt-warehouse</code>.</li>
<li>Check that the README renders, the Mermaid diagram draws, and images appear.</li>
<li>Click the <strong>Actions</strong> tab to see your CI run. If it failed, open it to read the log. Common causes are missing Kaggle secrets or a failing test.</li>
<li>Add the CI secrets (if using the Kaggle download step): <strong>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret</strong> for <code dir="ltr">KAGGLE_USERNAME</code> and <code dir="ltr">KAGGLE_KEY</code>.</li>
</ol>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Step 6: Polish the repo page</h4>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li>Click the gear icon next to <strong>About</strong>: add a one-line description and topics like <code dir="ltr">dbt</code>, <code dir="ltr">duckdb</code>, <code dir="ltr">data-engineering</code>, <code dir="ltr">analytics-engineering</code>.</li>
<li>Pin the repo on your GitHub profile: <strong>Customize your pins</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="ltr" aria-level="6">Common problems</h4>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><strong>Push rejected: file larger than 100 MB.</strong> You committed a data or database file. If it was in your latest commit, run <code dir="ltr">git rm --cached olist/olist.duckdb</code> (use the real path), then <code dir="ltr">git commit --amend --no-edit</code>, then push again, and add it to <code dir="ltr">.gitignore</code>. If it’s older than the last commit, paste the error and I’ll walk you through it.</li>
<li><strong><code dir="ltr">git push</code> says “rejected, fetch first”.</strong> Run <code dir="ltr">git pull --rebase</code> and then <code dir="ltr">git push</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Images don’t show.</strong> Check that the path and capitalization in the README match the file names exactly.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Part 4: Upload the Databricks project</h3>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>On GitHub: <strong>+ → New repository</strong>, name it <code dir="ltr">databricks-nyc-taxi-lakehouse</code>, Public, with a README, then <strong>Create</strong>.</li>
<li>Clone it: <code dir="ltr">git clone https://github.com/&lt;YOUR-USERNAME&gt;/databricks-nyc-taxi-lakehouse.git</code> and <code dir="ltr">cd</code> into it.</li>
<li>Create the folders and copy in your exported notebooks, pipeline files, screenshots, and the README above.</li>
<li>Run the same sequence: <code dir="ltr">git add .</code>, <code dir="ltr">git commit -m "Add Databricks NYC taxi lakehouse project"</code>, <code dir="ltr">git push</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>No-terminal alternative:</strong> on the repo page click <strong>Add file → Upload files</strong>, drag in your folders, and commit. It works well for a small project like this.</p>
<hr>
<h3 dir="ltr" aria-level="5">Final checklist before sharing the links</h3>
<ul dir="ltr" class="contains-task-list">
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> No <code dir="ltr">&lt;placeholders&gt;</code> or guessed numbers left in either README</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Every screenshot you reference exists in <code dir="ltr">docs/images/</code></li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Test counts and row counts match your actual runs</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> No secrets, data files, or <code dir="ltr">.duckdb</code> files committed</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> CI badge is green, or the README says what CI covers</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Repos are public and pinned on your profile</li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr">When your repos are live, I can help you write the resume bullets from your real results. Send me your test count, row counts, and what your dashboard showed.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ms-[calc(var(--cds-assistant-message-text-inset,0px)_-_6px)] touch:has-[&gt;[data-size=xs]&gt;:first-child:not(time)]:ms-[calc(var(--cds-assistant-message-text-inset,0px)_-_0.625rem*var(--cds-rem-scale,1))] print:mt-xs"><div data-cds="MessageActions" data-reveal="fade" role="toolbar" aria-label="Message actions" data-size="xs" tabindex="-1" class="flex items-center select-none touch:flex-wrap touch:[--cds-h-control--xs:calc(2rem*var(--cds-rem-scale,1))] touch:h-auto touch:min-h-[calc(1.5rem*var(--cds-rem-scale,1))] touch:gap-y-[calc(0.5rem*var(--cds-rem-scale,1))] touch:*:-my-[calc(0.25rem*var(--cds-rem-scale,1))] [&amp;_button]:text-muted [&amp;_button:hover:not([aria-pressed=true])]:text-primary stacks:[&amp;_button:not(:where([data-cds-theme]_*:not([data-cds-unthemed]_*)))]:[--cds-text-muted:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-plain-secondary)]!" data-testid="message-actions"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 rounded-[calc(var(--cds-radius)+var(--cds-button-radius-add,0px))] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]: